+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The optional :rst:directive:option:`canonical`
+   option supplies the alias expression, which is displayed after an equals
+   sign.  Names in the expression are parsed as Python type references.
+
+   The directive may be placed inside a class description to document a class
+   scoped alias.  Its body can contain a description, but the alias does not
+   create a further namespace.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: Python type expression
+
+      The alias expression.  Its type names are parsed as cross-references.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
